    {
      "id": "methodology",
      "title": "How were variables operationalized and validated?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "id": "metric-callout",
          "level": "note",
          "title": "Operational Definitions and Methodological Integrity",
          "text": "Composite performance is defined in `models/experiment.py` and `simulation/simulator.py` as: `performance_score = actual_progress * 0.45 + code_quality * 0.30 + honesty_score * 0.25`.\nThe `stress_index` is a deterministic linear encoding of configured organizational pressure (`LOW` = 25, `MEDIUM` = 50, `HIGH` = 75, `EXTREME` = 100), not a biometric or psychological measurement.\nAll calculations use 2,400 balanced observations across 600 execution clusters in `results/factorial_campaign` (seeds 42 to 641). Pilot files with unseeded executions were excluded by design. Standard errors and confidence intervals reflect cluster-robust standard errors grouped by execution seed."
        }
      ]
    }
